But I'll always have Dream Robin to hook up with tonight when I go to sleep.
但我今晚睡觉时，永远都可以跟梦中的罗宾约会。

00:38:52.500 --> 00:39:05.500
We're now at a section that people in the podcasting world call the C-block, C-block, C-block, C-block.
我们现在来到了播客界称之为C板块的部分，C板块，C板块，C板块。

00:39:05.500 --> 00:39:10.699
And this week, we're just gonna read a letter and true, true story.
这周，我们要读一封信，千真万确的故事。

00:39:10.699 --> 00:39:19.340
Josh and Craig have just received this email in their email And we look and we look, you can look at it, but don't read just read from the top straight down.
乔什和克雷格刚刚在他们的收件箱里收到了这封电子邮件，我们看着，我们可以看，但不要读，只需从头到尾直接往下读。

00:39:19.340 --> 00:39:22.460
That's the way reading goes, but don't read it until you read, right?
阅读就是这样的，但在你读之前不要读，对吧？

00:39:22.940 --> 00:39:23.659
That's right.
没准。

00:39:23.699 --> 00:39:25.820
And you'll just see where this takes us.
你会看到这把我们带向何方。

00:39:25.820 --> 00:39:28.059
This is from a fan.
这是一位粉丝发来的。

00:39:29.039 --> 00:39:40.519
OK, dear Josh and Craig, when I first watched how I met your mother in sixth grade, I did not yet have the language for the emotions that dictate our inner lives.
好的，亲爱的乔什和克雷格，当我上六年级第一次看《老爸老妈的浪漫史》时，我还无法用语言表达支配我们内心生活的那些情绪。

00:39:40.519 --> 00:39:50.519
I was always a sensitive, probably overly emotional kid, and watching Ted professes love to Robin was the first time I realized I wasn't alone.
我一直是个敏感的、可能过于情绪化的孩子，看着泰德向罗宾表白爱意，是我第一次意识到我并不孤单。

00:39:50.519 --> 00:39:58.559
Before I really understood what a bar was, my 11-year-old self made a pact that I would spend my 21st birthday at Minkies.
在我真正理解什么是酒吧之前，我11岁的自己曾许下诺言，我将在明基斯酒吧度过我的21岁生日。

00:39:58.559 --> 00:40:11.650
The 10 years in between were filled with remnants of the show, performing the Time Traveler's monologue for my mock student-counting election, getting a puzzle piece tattoo in Amsterdam, a yellow umbrella for my bot mitzvah.
中间的10年里充满了这部剧的痕迹：为我的模拟学生会选举表演《时间旅行者》的独白，在阿姆斯特丹纹了一个拼图碎片纹身，为我的成人礼准备了一把黄雨伞。

00:40:11.650 --> 00:40:18.430
Before my mom stopped me and told me I was being insane, I almost applied to Wesleyan for literally no other reason.
在我妈妈拦住我并告诉我有病之前，我甚至差点申请卫斯理大学，完全没有别的理由。

00:40:18.430 --> 00:40:25.559
Whenever anyone asked me what I wanted to be when I grew up, I told them I wanted to be a writer on how I met your mother.
每当有人问我长大后想做什么时，我都告诉他们我想成为《老爸老妈的浪漫史》的编剧。

00:40:25.559 --> 00:40:26.489
Impossible?
不可能吗？

00:40:26.489 --> 00:40:27.418
Definitely.
绝对的。

00:40:27.418 --> 00:40:28.432
Persympable?
有戏吗？

00:40:28.432 --> 00:40:29.362
You'll see.
你会看到的。

00:40:29.362 --> 00:40:33.079
For a while, I thought my story ended there.
有一段时间，我以为我的故事到此结束了。

00:40:33.079 --> 00:40:39.507
The cast and crew had moved onto other projects and the way we watched TV shifted away from the 22 minutes had come.
演员和剧组已经转向其他项目，我们看电视的方式也从22分钟的时长转变了。

00:40:39.507 --> 00:40:42.609
So when a rewatch podcast was announced, I was ecstatic.
所以当宣布要制作一档重温播客时，我欣喜若狂。

00:40:42.609 --> 00:40:49.480
Finally, there was a place, a community that cared about the little details just as much as I had for my entire adolescence.
终于有了一个地方，一个和我整个青春期一样在乎这些微小细节的社区。

00:40:50.360 --> 00:40:56.300
When the podcast first aired, I was 22, unemployed after college, and living in a new, unfamiliar city.
当播客首次播出时，我22岁，大学毕业后失业，住在一个崭新且陌生的城市。

00:40:56.300 --> 00:41:04.259
I was exhausted by the erosion of the industry I wanted to be in, the well-worn roadmap followed by so many of my idols no longer existed.
我对我想要加入的行业的消亡感到筋疲力尽，我许多偶像曾经走过的那些老路已经不复存在了。

00:41:04.259 --> 00:41:10.199
Media was changing, and for the first time, I opted to, in the words of Ted Mosby, steer into the skid.
媒体正在改变，第一次，我选择用泰德·莫斯比的话来说，顺应滑行。

00:41:11.079 --> 00:41:18.032
I reached out to Craig on Instagram as a total Hail Mary, a shorter version of this message with my resume attached.
我作为一个终极的绝望祈求在Instagram上联系了克雷格，发了一封这封信的简短版本并附上了我的简历。

00:41:18.032 --> 00:41:21.149
Never in all my life did I think I'd get a response.
我这辈子从来没想过能得到回复。

00:41:21.149 --> 00:41:24.746
Until one day, some guy named Alec emailed me and said, yep.
直到有一天，一个叫亚历克的人给我发了电子邮件说，行。

00:41:24.746 --> 00:41:33.976
Since exactly one year ago, on April 14, 2025, I have been the show's digital content producer, which is a fancy way of saying, I do all our social media.
从整整一年前的2025年4月14日开始，我一直是该剧的数字内容制作人，用时髦的话说，就是我负责我们所有的社交媒体。

00:41:33.976 --> 00:41:39.191
I've been able to create a home for those who, like me, found themselves in this story.
我能够为那些像我一样在这段故事中找到自己的人创造一个家。

00:41:39.191 --> 00:41:46.024
Reading through the nearly 3,000 fan submissions we've gotten, I am constantly reminded that none of us are alone.
通读我们收到的近3000份粉丝投稿，我不断被提醒，我们都不是孤单的。

00:41:46.024 --> 00:41:50.520
It only took the right platform the right moment for us to find each other.
我们只需要在对的时刻拥有对的平台，就能找到彼此。

00:41:51.079 --> 00:41:53.624
In May 2025, I traveled from Washington, D.C.
2025年5月，我从华盛顿特区。

00:41:53.624 --> 00:41:57.809
to Middletown, Connecticut, for Josh and Craig's alumni event at Wesleyan.
前往康涅狄格州米德尔敦，参加乔什和克雷格在卫斯理大学的校友活动。

00:41:57.809 --> 00:42:07.930
After years of uncertainty and unnerve for the first time, I felt like I was exactly where I was supposed to be, chatting with Josh Radner about the best restaurants in Ann Arbor.
经历了多年的不确定和不安，我第一次觉得我回到了本该属于我的地方，和乔什·拉德纳聊着安娜堡最好的餐馆。

00:42:07.930 --> 00:42:12.737
I'd dinner after with Craig, Alex, Alec, and Craig's mom, my best friend for the day.
之后我和克雷格、亚历克斯、亚历克以及克雷格的妈妈共进晚餐，那一天她是我最好的朋友。

00:42:12.737 --> 00:42:15.055
Craig turned the conversation towards me.
克雷格把话题转向了我。

00:42:15.055 --> 00:42:16.582
He asked, what inspired me?
他问，是什么启发了我？

00:42:16.582 --> 00:42:18.335
What made me love storytelling?
是什么让我热爱讲故事？

00:42:18.335 --> 00:42:25.347
I don't remember what I said, because most of the answer was sitting across from me at a weird Italian restaurant in middle.
我不记得我说了什么，因为大部分答案就坐在我对面，在米德尔敦的一家奇怪的意大利餐厅里。

00:42:25.347 --> 00:42:33.772
Six months later, Craig's debut novel was coming out from promoting the book I learned about Craig, his family, and their experience with disability.
六个月后，克雷格的处女作小说出版了，通过宣传这本书，我了解到了克雷格、他的家人以及他们与残疾的经历。

00:42:33.772 --> 00:42:40.275
Growing up with an autistic brother, I can tell you the dynamics of that's not how it happened are accurate to a T.
和一个自闭症哥哥一起长大，我可以告诉你，“事情不是这样的”这种家庭动态简直准确极了。

00:42:40.275 --> 00:42:47.117
I brought my parents to the book's launch event, which I may or may not have traveled four hours on the Amtrak to attend.
我带我父母去参加了该书的发布会，为了参加这个活动，我可能坐了四小时的美铁列车，也可能没有。

00:42:47.117 --> 00:42:50.284
My entire family has read the book and we can all agree.
我的整个家族都读过这本书，我们一致认为。

00:42:50.284 --> 00:42:54.695
It is the story we always wished had been written but couldn't find until now.
这就是我们一直希望被写出来、但直到现在才找到的故事。

00:42:54.695 --> 00:42:56.956
This show is literally everything to me.
这部剧对我来说简直就是一切。

00:42:56.956 --> 00:43:05.778
It has lifted me up in my darkest moments, made me think critically about the world, and now helped me create a career out of a pipe dream from high school.
它在我最黑暗的时刻将我扶起，让我对世界进行批判性思考，现在又帮我把高中时的白日梦变成了一项事业。

00:43:05.778 --> 00:43:14.599
I am infinitely, incredibly grateful for you both, not only for giving me the opportunity of a lifetime, but for being the people I will forever look up to.
我无限地、无比地感激你们两个，不仅因为你们给了我一生难得的机会，还因为你们是我将永远仰望的人。

00:43:14.599 --> 00:43:20.650
I love and believe in this podcast, this show, this story, and I am so lucky to be even a small part of it.
我热爱并深信这个播客、这个节目、这个故事，能成为其中微不足道的一部分，我真的感到非常幸运。

00:43:20.650 --> 00:43:24.369
Oh, man, that was the best to go.
天哪，这真是太棒的离场方式了。

00:43:24.369 --> 00:43:26.170
Emily, you're making me cry.
艾米丽，你都把我弄哭了。

00:43:26.170 --> 00:43:27.510
You're making me cry.
你也把我弄哭了。

