而且我们现在人手已经满了，你不能再抢一份工作。

00:45:09.150 --> 00:45:15.590
But no, I think it's a great lesson in like, let your passions lead you to the thing.
不过说真的，我认为这是一个很好的教训，那就是：让你的热情指引你走向目标。

00:45:15.590 --> 00:45:18.909
And also don't be afraid to inquire, you know?
还有，不要害怕去询问，你知道吗？

00:45:18.909 --> 00:45:24.269
Like, we actually were understaffed and served and needed some help, you know what I mean?
因为我们当时其实人手不足、服务不够，确实需要一些帮助，你知道我的意思吗？

00:45:24.269 --> 00:45:26.190
Like you, so thank you.
所以，谢谢你。

00:45:26.190 --> 00:45:30.469
Yeah, take the shot, like shoot your shot and you did, and we could tell us from the heart.
对，勇敢尝试，放手一搏，你确实这么做了，而且我们能看出这是出自真心的。

00:45:30.469 --> 00:45:32.989
And it's been so great to work with you.
能和你共事真的太棒了。

00:45:32.989 --> 00:45:37.670
And again, like, you're the kind of person that we hoped was watching this thing we were making.
还有，就像我说的，你正是我们所希望的、会观看我们制作的这个节目的人。

00:45:37.670 --> 00:45:39.710
And it turned out you were out there on the other side.
结果证明，你就在世界的另一端。

00:45:39.710 --> 00:45:41.230
We didn't know you yet.
虽然我们还不认识你。

00:45:41.230 --> 00:45:44.349
But you made sure there would be a way that we'd get to know you.
但你确保了总有一天我们会认识你。

00:45:44.349 --> 00:45:45.469
And I'm so glad that we do.
我很高兴我们真的做到了。

00:45:45.469 --> 00:45:51.150
And I just want to say thank you for those kinds of words about my book and you and your family have said such nice things to me about the book.
我只想对你关于我的书的那些赞美表示感谢，你和你的家人也曾对我说过很多关于这本书的暖心话。

00:45:51.150 --> 00:45:55.150
I'm again, you're my target audience for that story too.
我再次觉得，你也是那个故事的目标受众。

00:45:55.150 --> 00:45:58.829
And it means the world to me that it connected with you guys truly.
它能与你们产生共鸣，对我来说意义重大，真的。

00:45:58.829 --> 00:45:59.670
So thanks.
所以谢谢你们。

00:45:59.670 --> 00:46:01.309
Thank you for all of you both.
谢谢你们所有人。

00:46:01.309 --> 00:46:08.630
Did you ever think about like, I'm not going to even bother reaching out, it's too much of a long shot.
你有没有想过，“算了吧，我甚至懒得去联系，成功的几率太渺茫了”？

00:46:08.630 --> 00:46:13.829
But like, when you reached out, did it feel like a bajillion, was it like Project Hail Mary?
但是，当你迈出这一步时，是不是觉得希望渺茫，就像电影《极地求生》里那样？

00:46:13.829 --> 00:46:14.829
Was it like, this is never going to happen?
是不是觉得：这根本不可能发生？

00:46:14.829 --> 00:46:17.150
But you just like, what made you do that?
但你还是做了，是什么促使你这么做的？

00:46:17.150 --> 00:46:19.710
Like, you just like, it worked.
结果竟然成功了。

00:46:19.710 --> 00:46:20.710
You actually did it.
你真的做到了。

00:46:20.710 --> 00:46:21.710
You did the thing.
你完成了这件事。

00:46:21.710 --> 00:46:25.190
But when you sent us that message, you must have thought this is going into the void, right?
但当你给我们发那条消息时，你一定觉得自己是在对虚空喊话吧？

00:46:25.190 --> 00:46:26.190
Yeah.
是的。

00:46:26.190 --> 00:46:34.690
I mean, most things have like, I feel like I, everyone my age has been applying the like hundreds of jobs and they're all on LinkedIn and half of them are fake anyway.
我的意思是，大多数事情都是这样，我觉得，我身边的每个人都在申请几百个工作岗位，它们全在领英（LinkedIn）上，而且其中有一半都是假的。

00:46:34.690 --> 00:46:37.849
And I was like, I was like, that's really not working.
当时我就想，我觉得这根本行不通。

00:46:38.210 --> 00:46:38.570
Yeah.
是的。

00:46:38.570 --> 00:46:42.140
And one of my friends sent me the podcast and was like, Emily, you have to listen to this.
我的一个朋友把这个播客发给我，并说：“艾米丽，你一定要听听这个。”

00:46:42.140 --> 00:46:43.409
And that was before it came out.
那是在节目正式上线之前。

00:46:43.690 --> 00:46:46.409
So I already had it in my head that like this was like my thing.
所以我心里早就认定，这就是我命中注定的东西。

00:46:46.409 --> 00:46:47.889
And I was so excited about it.
我对它充满了热情。

00:46:48.250 --> 00:46:49.809
And what's what people had told me about it.
也对别人向我讲述的关于它的种种感到兴奋。

00:46:49.809 --> 00:46:51.889
And I just felt like, why not?
我当时就觉得，为什么不试试呢？

00:46:52.170 --> 00:47:00.969
I also remember thinking like I submitted a fan message and I'm really glad I also direct message you because now that I've access to the fan messages, I know that there's 3,000 of them.
我也记得当时想过，我提交了一条粉丝留言，但我真的很高兴我也直接给你们发了私信，因为现在我有权查看粉丝留言了，我知道那里有3000条留言。

00:47:00.969 --> 00:47:03.610
So for how did I reach out to you directly?
所以如果我不直接联系你们怎么行呢？

00:47:03.610 --> 00:47:06.289
Yeah, no, and we had other people reach out.
对，没错，而且确实有其他人联系过我们。

00:47:06.289 --> 00:47:09.610
We had other people message us too, for whatever reason.
出于各种原因，也有其他人给我们发过消息。

00:47:09.610 --> 00:47:12.449
We just felt like, I don't know, she seems like the right person.
我们只是觉得，不知道为什么，她看起来就是那个对的人。

00:47:12.449 --> 00:47:17.469
Just like it was a weird little magical energy thing that when something's right, you kind of sense it.
就像是一种奇妙的小魔力，当某件事是对的时候，你自然能感觉得到。

00:47:17.469 --> 00:47:18.550
So it is cool.
所以这真的很酷。

00:47:18.550 --> 00:47:19.690
I think there's a cool lesson there.
我觉得这里面有一个很棒的道理。

00:47:19.690 --> 00:47:23.489
But I think it's so interesting to think about the show from like a Gen Z perspective.
但我认为，从Z世代（Gen Z）的视角来思考这部剧，是一件非常有趣的事情。

00:47:23.489 --> 00:47:26.170
And I know Josh has talked at this, how it's very analog.
我知道乔希也谈到过这一点，这部剧具有很强的复古模拟感。

00:47:26.170 --> 00:47:28.050
And I think it's just so timeless in that way.
我觉得它在这一点上永不过时。

00:47:28.050 --> 00:47:38.429
It's been really interesting to see my generation who doesn't really have as much of a TV presence yet kind of latch onto the show, and it's so cool to watch from here.
看到我的这一代人——他们目前在电视上的存在感还不算太强——开始喜欢并关注这部剧，真的非常有趣，从这个角度看过去感觉太棒了。

00:47:38.429 --> 00:47:45.369
Yeah, and maybe liking the comfort of a time that was a little bit simpler, although it makes it so very old, I also kind of like it.
对，也许是喜欢那种稍微简单一点的旧时光带来的慰藉吧，尽管这让我显得非常老气，但我其实也挺喜欢这种感觉的。

00:47:45.369 --> 00:47:46.489
Emily, that was amazing.
艾米丽，太精彩了。

00:47:46.489 --> 00:47:47.329
Bravo.
太棒了。

00:47:47.329 --> 00:47:48.489
Thank you, Emily.
谢谢你，艾米丽。

00:47:48.489 --> 00:47:49.650
We're happy you're here.
我们很高兴你能来。

00:47:49.650 --> 00:47:50.530
Yeah, we are.
是的，我们很高兴。

00:47:50.530 --> 00:47:52.130
Thank you.
谢谢你们。

00:47:52.130 --> 00:47:54.539
I am guilty.
我有罪。

00:47:54.539 --> 00:47:56.420
Please equip me.
请宣判我无罪吧。

00:47:56.420 --> 00:48:01.199
All sins are forgiven in New York City.
在纽约市，所有的罪孽都可以被原谅。

